    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d745">

                <pb facs="0707" n="609" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg609"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Choate to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1900-04-11"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April 11, 1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 300.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to Mr. White’s dispatch No.
                    283 of the 15th ultimo, I have the honor to transmit herewith the copy of a note
                    which has just been received from Her Majesty’s secretary of state for foreign
                    affairs in relation to the consignment of flour shipped by the Pennsylvania
                    Milling Company on board the steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Maria.</hi></p>
                <pb facs="0708" n="610" xml:id="pg610"/>
                <p>I am, for the moment, unable to obtain further information as to the details of
                    the transaction therein referred to, but assume that they will be perfectly
                    intelligible to the company.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph H. Choate.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d745-a1.xml" xpointer="d745-a1"/>
            </div>
